#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The Severn: the battle of 25 March 1655, Maryland.  A sample game for
the Grognard engine.

England's civil wars reach the Chesapeake.  The Puritans of Providence
have taken the government of Lord Baltimore's colony, and the governor
they put out, William Stone, has come up the bay with Baltimore's men
and their Piscataway allies to take it back.  He has landed on a wooded
neck by the mouth of the Severn; William Fuller is marching out to meet
him, under a flag borrowed from the merchant ship Golden Lyon.  Play
either side against the computer, or against a friend at the same
screen.

Run it with ./severn (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.severn.json.  ./severn --selftest checks the map and plays a
game between two computer players.
"""

